<p>
Each <code>config/tradelists/trader-&lt;specialization&gt;.json</code> (and
<code>villager-&lt;name&gt;.json</code>) file is a flat <code>{money, selling, buying}</code>
object; entries repeating the same item under different cosmetic <code>attributes</code> (e.g. a
tapestry listed many times under different "type" values) are collapsed to one listing, since
those variations are randomized/cosmetic rather than distinct tradeable things.
</p>
<p>
There's no list of "who trades what" anywhere -- an entity's own <code>attributes.tradePropsFile</code>
(or its glob-keyed <code>tradePropsFileByType</code>) names the tradelist file, with <code>{group}</code>
placeholders filled in from that variant's variant groups. Wandering traders use
<code>config/tradelists/trader-{type}</code>, where the <code>type</code> state <em>is</em> the specialization;
<code>villager.json</code> maps each named villager with <code>tradePropsFileByType</code>
(<code>*-tobias</code> &rarr; <code>villager-tobias</code>; Liga and Arzhur share <code>villager-liga</code>). Every
concrete entity variant resolving to a loaded list is linked back to it (and its creature page links here).
A listing of the generic <code>clutter</code> block links to the clutter type it names (its <code>type</code> attribute), e.g. Tobias's lanterns and books.
</p>
